835 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 348 0 R
/T (The study by Barbosa et al. \(2015\) "Comparison of Land, Water, and Energy Requirements of Lettuce Grown Using Hydroponic vs. Conventional Agricultural Methods" confirms that hydroponics reduces water consumption by over 90% while using very little space, but highlights a technical criticality: the energy required for water recirculation and climate control is up to 80 times higher than traditional agriculture, risking greater pollution if powered by fossil fuels. However, to adequately assess the system's true sustainability, a broader life cycle perspective must be adopted.)
/E (The study by Barbosa et al. \(2015\) "Comparison of Land, Water, and Energy Requirements of Lettuce Grown Using Hydroponic vs. Conventional Agricultural Methods" confirms that hydroponics reduces water consumption by over 90% while using very little space, but highlights a technical criticality: the energy required for water recirculation and climate control is up to 80 times higher than traditional agriculture, risking greater pollution if powered by fossil fuels. However, to adequately assess the system's true sustainability, a broader life cycle perspective must be adopted.)
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [3]
>>
